extraction_notes: "WB9 South America 2 printed 188-190 (cache p188-p190, page_offset 0); the introduction runs 188-189, abilities 1-6 are printed 189 and ability 7 onward, with the stat block, printed 190. Printed 189 and 190 checked against 110 dpi renders, which agreed with the OCR on every number (the OCR''s ''Sth'' is 5th, ''Al!'' is All). || XP: the Larhold Shaman / Pucara Mind Mage / Sun Priest ladder on printed 192, as briefed. || GROUP: magic. mdc_base is stated, so no men_of_arms line. || RACE: no race_restrictions. Printed 189 says shamans can belong to races other than the Larhold - humans, ogres, wolfen and others - and ability 7 prices both an M.D.C. race and an S.D.C. one. || POOLS: M.D.C. P.E. plus 1D4 per level, stored as mdc_base - the minor M.D.C. creature a human or other S.D.C. being becomes. A race that states its own mdc_base (the Larhold R.C.C.) keeps its pool in a pairing and this one is dropped, which is the book''s reading; the +10 M.D.C. that race gets instead is a choose-one ability carrying bonuses.pools.mdc 10, beside a prose-only S.D.C. option, because an unconditional pool bonus would also reach a human. P.P.E. 3D6x10 plus P.E., +3D6 per level. || BONUSES stored: +3 vs horror factor. The +1 to spell strength at 4, 7, 10 and 13 is level_progression prose - no spell strength field exists on the sheet. || MAGIC: type spell. Eight at creation as two starting groups: three from a named list of the ten Blue Flame spells (any level) and five from spell levels 1-2. Level two: four from levels 1-3 as a schedule entry, whose ''or any Blue Flame spells'' cannot be expressed beside a level gate and sits in its note. Levels 3-15: two per level, up_to_character_level. spell_traditions_allowed blue-flame, so level-gated picks reach the Blue Flame spells within their level caps (the book''s ''from any of the levels''); a consequence is that Sense Blue Flame (level 1) is also reachable from the five common picks. Spells cannot be learned or bought: a restriction. The Blue Flame spells are this book''s rows (#1390), names as the p.190 list prints them. || SKILLS: Language: Larhold 98 (fixed; no literacy printed). Language of choice +25 as a Language: Other pick. Basic and Advanced Math (+25%) as Mathematics: Basic 45+25 and Mathematics: Advanced 45+25. Demon and Monster Lore is Lore: Demons & Monsters 25+15. Riding: War Bison 50+10. Holistic Medicine 20+10. Wilderness Survival 30+5. W.P. Archery and Targeting as W.P. Archery; W.P. Sword. Hand to Hand: Basic to Expert for one other skill, to Martial Arts or Assassin for two; no alignment condition printed. || RELATED: six, plus one at levels 3, 5, 8, 12 and 14; the book says new skills start at the base skill level. Communications, Espionage, Medical, Physical, Pilot, Pilot Related, Rogue, W.P. and Wilderness any; Domestic +10; Science +5; Technical +10; Electrical, Mechanical and Military none. SECONDARY: three each at levels 1, 4 and 9. || EQUIPMENT: demon-mask, larhold-hide-armor, larhold-composite-bow and larhold-saber are this book''s rows (#1392); the bow row records the differing figures each class prints (+3 M.D. and P.S. 18 or robot P.S. 30 on this page). Shaman Robes as robe. One energy weapon of choice, 1D4 E-clips and one modern weapon as catalog choices. War Bison mount or small vehicle as on the R.C.C.; the robot horse has no row. Camping kit, two weeks of dry rations (qty 2 of emergency-food-rations) and cooking utensils as on the R.C.C. The holistic medicine bag has no suitable row (medical-bag is an unfilled stub for a modern kit) and is not stored or stubbed. The magic weapon granted at third level is level_progression prose. || MONEY: 2D6x1000 credits in cash or trade items, stored as 2d6x1000. In a pairing with the Larhold R.C.C., which states 1D6x1000, the race''s figure wins. || WARNING: class-check reports mdc_base, ppe_base and starting_money as fields a race stating its own would discard. Not supersedes_race - the book does not say the character stops being its race. mdc_base and starting_money are discarded as the book intends or harmlessly (above). ppe_base is NOT harmless: the Larhold R.C.C. states P.P.E. 3D6 (printed 186, the figure for a Larhold with no magical O.C.C.), so a Larhold shaman composes to 3D6 P.P.E. instead of this page''s 3D6x10 plus P.E., +3D6 per level. Recorded, not worked around; a human shaman (no race) gets the printed figure. Not stored differently; see BOOK-INGEST-AUDIT.md F111 (it also covers the 2D6x1000 starting money the race''s 1D6x1000 replaces). || Cybernetics: none."
