## Lore

The Larhold homeworld was a green-skied plain that crackled with the Blue
Flame, an elemental power almost unknown elsewhere in the Megaverse. Some of
the first Larhold sages bound themselves to it mystically and became shamans,
its priests; others worked out spells anyone with the gift could learn. No one
wields the Flame as well as a shaman.

True shamans hide behind demonic masks, bandages and cloaks, partly to cover
bodies scarred by the Flame and partly to inspire dread; only a true shaman may
wear the mask, and another shaman sees through any impostor. They heal the
tribe, aid its warriors, divine the outcome of battles, open the Rifts the
tribes travel by, and often fuel their magic with sacrificial victims. They are
also the tribe''s most skilled torturers, which has made them the most hated
Larhold of all, and a cornered shaman may call down the Flame to consume
himself and everyone around him.

The Flame itself is neither good nor evil. A few shamans live apart from the
tribes, and humans, ogres, wolfen and others have been taught the Ways of the
Flame.

## GM Notes

The Larhold also call ley line walkers, witches, warlocks and other magicians
"shamans"; only the priests of the gods of darkness rival the true shamans.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'larhold-shaman');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'larhold-shaman';

